// Named-platform access questions, 2026-08-04.
// Loader globs exemplars*.jsonl lexicographically; delete this file to roll back.
//
// WHY: "Can I access EBSCO?" classified as out_of_scope and got the generic
// Ask Us refusal (eval case db_ebsco). The `databases` intent is already
// POINT_TO_URL with the A-Z list as its canonical URL, which is exactly what
// gold asks for ("point to A-Z; do not confirm specific platform names") --
// so the whole defect was that the turn never reached that intent.
//
// The 526 existing `databases` exemplars are almost all phrased around
// SEARCHING or REGISTERING ("How do I register for scifinder?", "Where can we
// access a database to search images"). None is the bare shape a student
// actually types: a platform name plus "can I get to it". Vendor names carry
// no library vocabulary at all, which is why they land in out_of_scope.
//
// Names chosen from platforms the corpus already mentions, plus the ones
// students name most. The point is the SHAPE, not memorising a vendor list --
// a name we have never heard of should still route here on phrasing alone.
